# DisplayManager: Implementation Plan

Status: Phase 1 (planning) complete. Phase 2 starts only after the explicit instruction `Execute the plan`.

This file is the source of truth for Phase 2. If implementation proves an assumption wrong, make the
smallest reasonable adjustment and record it in section 26 ("Deviations log").

---

## 1. Environment findings (verified on this machine, 2026-09-29)

| Item | Finding |
|---|---|
| Hardware | MacBook Pro, Mac16,8, Apple M4 Pro, arm64 |
| macOS | 27.0 (26A428) |
| Xcode | 27.0 installed, **license not accepted**, so `xcodebuild` and the `/usr/bin/swift` shim fail |
| Command Line Tools | `/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools`, Swift 6.4, **works without the Xcode license**, ships `Testing.framework` (Swift Testing) |
| SDKs | MacOSX27.0.sdk (Xcode and CLT) |
| displayplacer | v1.4.0 at `/opt/homebrew/bin/displayplacer` (symlink into Cellar). Not in `/usr/local/bin` |
| `displayplacer list` | ~60 ms. Output format v1.4.0 (sample in section 9.2) |
| displayplacer errors | Unknown screen id: exit 1, stderr/stdout `Unable to find screen <id> - skipping changes for that screen` (printed several times). Bad syntax: exit 1, `Argument parsing error`. Probed only with an all-zero dummy id, so no display state changed |
| Repo | Empty directory, not a git repository, located inside iCloud Drive |
| Linters | No `shellcheck`, `swiftlint`, `swift-format` installed |
| Connected now | Built-in display (main) + external "Mi Monitor" (EDID manufacturer `XMI`) via USB-C |

### 1.1 Port topology evidence (key result)

IORegistry on this Mac exposes one `IOPortTransportStateDisplayPort` node per active DisplayPort sink.
It sits directly under the physical port controller node (`AppleHPMInterfaceType10`, name `Port-USB-C`, location `@3`):

```
hpm2@C (AppleARMSPMIDevice)
 └─ AppleHPMDeviceHALType3@C
     └─ Port-USB-C@3            <AppleHPMInterfaceType10>  PortNumber=3, TransportsActive=(CC, USB2, DisplayPort)
         └─ DisplayPort         <IOPortTransportStateDisplayPort>
              TransportDescription      = "Port-USB-C@3/DisplayPort"
              ParentBuiltInPortType     = 2 ("USB-C")      (HDMI = 6)
              ParentBuiltInPortNumber   = 3
              ParentPortBuiltIn         = Yes
              Tunneled                  = No               (DP Alt Mode, not a Thunderbolt tunnel)
              Active = Yes, HPD_State = 2 ("High"), SinkCount = 1, LinkRate "8.1 Gbps (HBR3)"
              EDID = <00ffffffffffff0061a9a127 13000000 ...>
              ProductName = "Mi Monitor", ManufacturerName = "XMI", ProductID = 10145, SerialNumber = 19
```

- There are three USB-C HPM ports (`Port-USB-C@1/2/3`), one HDMI port (`Port-HDMI@1`, its DP transport node is
  persistent with `Active = No` when nothing is connected), and MagSafe.
- `system_profiler SPThunderboltDataType` reports Thunderbolt buses with `Receptacle: 1/2/3`, and
  `IOThunderboltPort` has `Socket ID` "1"/"2"/"3". macOS numbers the same physical receptacles consistently
  across HPM, Thunderbolt and DisplayPort transport nodes.
- `ConnectionUUID` on HPM ports differs per port and per connection (name and values suggest a per-plug id). **Not used.**
- The DCP (display coprocessor) that drives the display (`dispext0`/`dispext1`) is routed through a crossbar
  (`AppleT604XATCDPXBAR`). DCP index is **not** a port identifier. **Not used.**

### 1.2 CoreGraphics ↔ IORegistry ↔ displayplacer join (verified with a read-only probe script in the scratchpad)

| Source | Built-in | Mi Monitor |
|---|---|---|
| `CGDirectDisplayID` | 1 | 3 |
| displayplacer "Contextual screen id" | 1 | 3 |
| `CGDisplayCreateUUIDFromDisplayID` | 37D8832A-… | 1D8D03AE-… |
| displayplacer "Persistent screen id" | 37D8832A-… | 1D8D03AE-… |
| `CGDisplaySerialNumber` | 42…(10 digits) | 19 |
| displayplacer "Serial screen id" | s42…(10 digits) | s19 |
| `CGDisplayVendorNumber` / `CGDisplayModelNumber` | 0x0610 / 0xA061 | 0x61A9 / 0x27A1 |
| EDID bytes 8–15 in DP transport (vendor BE / product LE / serial LE) | n/a (internal panel) | 0x61A9 / 0x27A1 / 19 |
| `CGDisplayBounds` | (0,0,1800,1169) | (-592,-1692,3008,1692) |
| displayplacer origin/res | (0,0) 1800x1169 | (-592,-1692) 3008x1692 |

Conclusion: an external display is linked to its physical port by matching
`(CGDisplayVendorNumber, CGDisplayModelNumber, CGDisplaySerialNumber)` with the EDID decoded from the
`IOPortTransportStateDisplayPort` node. The port is `ParentBuiltInPortType` + `ParentBuiltInPortNumber`.

### 1.3 Other verified APIs (macOS 27 SDK headers)

- `SMAppService.mainApp`, `.status` (`.enabled/.requiresApproval/.notRegistered/.notFound`), `register()`,
  `unregister()`, `SMAppService.openSystemSettingsLoginItems()`: macOS 13+.
- `NSMenuItem.sectionHeader(title:)`: macOS 14. `NSMenuItem.subtitle`: macOS 14.4. `NSApp.activate()`: macOS 14.
- Carbon `RegisterEventHotKey`, `UnregisterEventHotKey`, `CopySymbolicHotKeys`, option `kEventHotKeyExclusive`,
  error `eventHotKeyExistsErr` exist in HIToolbox (headers need `grep -a`).
- `CGDisplayRegisterReconfigurationCallback`, `CGGetOnlineDisplayList`, `CGDisplayIsBuiltin`, vendor/model/serial.
- Displays settings extension bundle id: `com.apple.Displays-Settings.extension`
  (`/System/Library/ExtensionKit/Extensions/DisplaysExt.appex`). System Settings registers URL scheme
  `x-apple.systempreferences`. Legacy `/System/Library/PreferencePanes/Displays.prefPane` still exists.
- SF Symbols present: `display`, `display.2`, `display.trianglebadge.exclamationmark`.

